'''Rats''' are small animals commonly found throughout [[Gielinor]], mostly in cities, [[sewer]]s, and [[dungeon]]s. They respawn rapidly, and are not marked on the minimap.

Although most rats have no drops, the rats in the [[Stronghold of Security]] have a 100% chance to drop [[bones]] when killed by the player.

Considered by most players to be the weakest [[monster]] in the game, rats are frequently used to train [[Magic]] by [[splashing]].[[File:Rat idle animation.gif|thumb|right|Rat idle animation.]]

==Cats==
Rats can be chased by [[Cat|cats]]. When telling a cat to ''chase vermin'', it will pounce at a rat in range, attempting to catch it. If your cat successfully catches at least 100 rats, you can talk to [[Gertrude]] to get a [[cat training medal]], which has no special uses other than being a collectible. Furthermore, if you have a [[rat pole]], up to six caught rats can be added to it as decoration.

Each type of cat has a different catch rate:

*[[Kitten]] - 10% (temporarily increased to 40% during [[Ratcatchers]])
*[[Cat|Normal]] - 50% (temporarily increased to 70% during Ratcatchers)
*[[Overgrown cat|Overgrown]] - 0% (cannot chase rats, but can fight the [[King rat]])
*[[Wily cat|Wily]] - 50% + separate 12.5% to 50% roll, depending on [[Wily cat#Training|activity level]]
*[[Lazy cat|Lazy]] - 33% + separate 12.5% to 100% roll, depending on [[Lazy cat#Training|activity level]] ('''Note:''' It is not possible for lazy cats to reach maximum activity level, as they will turn back into wily cats before reaching it.)

[[Hellcat|Hellcats]] share the same catch rates as regular cats, depending on their type.

